    "updated_at": "2023-03-21T21:02:03Z",
    "body": "I got this far in my `starship.toml` config file (where `\\u001b` is the escape byte):\r\n\r\n```\r\n[directory]\r\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;http://example.com\\u001b\\\\\\\\This is a link\\u001b\\\\]8;;\\u001b\\\\\\\\ \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis creates a hyperlink that looks like this: [This is a link](http://example.com)\r\n\r\nHowever, I haven't been able to inject `[$path]` successfully. This config:\r\n```\r\n[directory]\r\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;[$path]\\u001b\\\\\\\\[$path]\\u001b\\\\]8;;\\u001b\\\\\\\\ \"\r\n```\r\nresults in the following error in starship 1.13.1:\r\n```\r\n[WARN] - (starship::modules::directory): Error in module `directory`:\r\n --> 1:13\r\n  |\r\n1 | ]8;;[$path]\\[$path]]8;;\\\r\n  |             ^---\r\n  |\r\n  = expected variable, string, textgroup, or conditional\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
