    "updated_at": "2024-05-13T07:11:43Z",
    "body": "Based on @lucaspimentel 's idea, Here's my workaround for this using custom commands:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n${custom.pwd_link_start}\\\r\n$directory\\\r\n${custom.pwd_link_end}\\\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[custom.pwd_link_start]\r\ncommand = 'echo %cd%'  # Change this for other shells or OS\r\nwhen = true\r\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;[file:$output]()\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\r\n\r\n[custom.pwd_link_end]\r\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\r\nwhen = true\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tested it with Clink on Windows and it works fine. It should work with other shells as well after some necessary modifications.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/starship/starship/assets/35839367/b2d48e66-e7e6-437f-982d-72559f94c167)\r\n\r\nYou may also want to try using only `directory ` with `[file:$path]()`, however `$path` is just the literal truncated path (*as is*) which makes it less useful in file protocol. If the starship team could add something like `$full_path` or `$real_path` that would be great.",
