    "updated_at": "2026-01-12T11:22:58Z",
    "body": "This took me probably longer than it should, but I just recently started my powershell journey so its ok.\n\nBased on @zyf722 's idea, I just wanted to try it out myself and havent got it working at first, because I just do not know toml at all and implemented it the wrong way a thousand times.\n\nThen `echo %cd%` didn't worked for me and I installed posh, where I first saw that feature, uninstalled it again and got back to starship.\n\n\nI got it working ( For everyone just as unexperienced as me, you have to sandwich the \n```\nformat = \"\"\"\n${custom.pwd_link_start}\\\n$directory\\\n${custom.pwd_link_end}\\\n\"\"\"\n```\ninto your existing toml \"format\" like so:\n```\nformat = \"\"\"\n[░▒▓](#2e3440)\\\n$os\\\n$username\\\n[](bg:#3b4252 fg:#2e3440)\\\n**${custom.pwd_link_start}\\**\n$directory\\\n**${custom.pwd_link_end}\\**\n[](fg:#3b4252 bg:#434c5e)\\\n....\n...\n```\n\nThis took me 5 minutes to realize why I get these errors, \"format is used too often etc\".\n\nAfter that, I got a non-functional URI with `%cd%`\n\n```\n[custom.pwd_link_start]\ncommand = 'echo %cd%'  # **Change this for other shells or OS** _I know, but what is it on pwsh lmao?_\nwhen = true\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;[file:$output]()\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\n\n[custom.pwd_link_end]\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\nwhen = true\n```\n\n<img width=\"323\" height=\"183\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/43894a48-7c0b-4dd3-9af2-e168148f123b\" />\n\n\nAfter that, I tried to figure out how to force PWSH to just give me back my current \"dir\" as a string without any tables or objects etc.\n\n\nThe thing I found and came up with @zyf722 code snipped and Get-Helping my ass out of this is as follows:\n\n```\n[custom.pwd_link_start]\ncommand = '(Get-Location).Path'  # Change this for other shells or OS\nwhen = true\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;[$output]()\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\n\n[custom.pwd_link_end]\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\nwhen = true\n```\n\nYou have to put this just below the format part in your toml.\n\n<img width=\"326\" height=\"117\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc30f6d8-507a-48d1-b54b-95ae82cdf7cd\" />\n\nIt took me tooooo long to figure it out because I am a newb at this to the limit. I just thought, If anyone out there wants to modify their starship.rs toml config so it can **HyperLink** your **Path** / **Directory** out of **Powershell 7** \n\nAND the best part is,it works in VS Code too!\n\n<img width=\"163\" height=\"53\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/80e86d39-29fc-45ff-8cac-7466e362a24d\" />\n\nI am probably too proud for this copy nightmare , but here we go I guess\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
