    "updated_at": "2026-04-12T21:49:53Z",
    "body": "If anyone is interested in having this work in PS 7 or PS 5 or CMD or BASH, most shells on windows anyway.  I created a simple batch file that most shells can run that returns the current directory and placed it in my path.\n\nSo currentdirectory.bat contains\n@echo off\necho %cd%\n\nPlace that file somewhere in your path\n\nthen in starship.toml\nchange the command for custom.pwd_link_start to call currentdirectory.bat\n\n[custom.pwd_link_start]\ncommand = 'currentdirectory.bat'  # This works in most shells on Windows\nwhen = true\nformat = \"\\u001b\\\\]8;;[$output]()\\u001b\\\\\\\\\"\n\nAnd this will have it working in most shells\n",
